  "reason": "The records collectively point toward thermally induced structural evolution in high-entropy alloys, possible departures from sluggish diffusion, kinetic rather than purely entropy-based control, and measurable surface diffusion in Au nanoparticles using aberration-corrected electron microscopy. They also contain related ideas about phase separation, nanoparticle surface stabilization, thermal processing, and non-equilibrium HEA formation. However, none identifies the specific combination of in situ vacuum heating of sub-10-nm AuCoCuNiPt particles, surface-energy-driven Au/Cu segregation, reshaping-enhanced diffusion, and subsequent selective evaporation. An expert could infer that heated HEA nanoparticles merit direct diffusion and stability measurements, but predicting the particular intervention and mechanism would require a substantial additional idea."
